  "content": "<html><head></head><body><p><a href=\"https://laravel-news.com/laravel-scheduler-multiple-servers\"></a></p>\n                                        <hr>\n\n                    <p>Laravel 13.35 adds Schedule::alwaysOnOneServer() to run every task once across servers, and a way for long scheduled commands to stop during a deploy.</p>\n\n                    <p>The post <a href=\"https://laravel-news.com/laravel-scheduler-multiple-servers\">Running Laravel's Scheduler on Multiple Servers</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://laravel-news.com\">Laravel News</a>.</p>\n                    <p>Join the <a href=\"https://laravel-news.com/newsletter\">Laravel Newsletter</a> to get <a href=\"https://laravel-news.com\">Laravel</a> articles like this directly in your inbox.</p>\n\n                    </body></html>",
